  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "Cross-Chain Governance is a coordination framework and set of protocols that enable governance proposals, voting outcomes, and policy updates to propagate and be enforced across multiple heterogeneous blockchain networks without requiring a single trusted intermediary. It extends on-chain governance mechanisms \u2014 token-weighted voting, quadratic voting, time-locked execution \u2014 to multi-chain environments using interoperability layers such as IBC (Inter-Blockchain Communication), cross-chain message passing bridges, or relay networks. Achieving consistent governance state across chains requires solving distributed consensus problems whilst preserving each chain's sovereignty.",
